{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the physicians embalmed him.</b> The nature of embalming was that they would compound him with spices and kinds of aromatics, in the manner of what is written concerning King Asa (II Chronicles 16:14): ״וישכיבהו במשכב אשר מלא בשמים וזנים מרקחים במרקחת מעשה״, and this was after the washing. And the sense of ויחנטו is that they gave orders to do so, for they were expert in the science of nature; the physicians did not handle his body themselves."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:47.100704617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}